# Part B — Supplemental Terms (Licensor)

These Supplemental Terms are provided by the Licensor under the "Notices"
section of Part A. They narrow the permitted purposes of the PolyForm
Noncommercial License so that free use of this software is limited to
**individual personal use**, and they add disclaimers specific to trading
software.

## B.1 Permitted Personal Use (Free)

Free use of the software is limited to **personal use by an individual natural
person**. Your use is permitted without payment only if **all** of the
following conditions are met:

- You are an individual natural person (not a company, partnership, LLC,
  corporation, fund, trust, or any other entity or organization), using the
  software for your own personal account; and
- You are managing less than **USD $5,000,000** in aggregate trading capital
  or assets under management ("AUM") across all accounts you trade with the
  software; and
- You are not providing trading, advisory, consulting, or other services to
  any third party using the software.

This is the controlling condition for free use. The barrier is **personal
use** — not merely "noncommercial" use.

## B.2 Entity and Organizational Use Is Not Free

Notwithstanding the "Noncommercial Purposes," "Personal Uses," and
"Noncommercial Organizations" provisions of Part A, **any use by or on behalf
of an entity or organization is not permitted free of charge** and requires a
separate Commercial License. This includes, without limitation, use by or for:

- Any company, partnership, LLC, corporation, sole proprietorship, fund, or
  trust — **including a small or two-person entity**; and
- Any charitable organization, educational institution, public research
  organization, public safety or health organization, environmental protection
  organization, or government institution.

If two or more people use the software together, or if anyone uses it on behalf
of an entity, that use is beyond Personal Use and requires a Commercial
License, regardless of whether the use is commercial.

## B.3 Uses Requiring a Commercial License

A separate, paid **Commercial License** from the Licensor is required for any
use that is not Permitted Personal Use under Section B.1, including:

- Any use by or on behalf of an entity or organization (see Section B.2);
- Managing or controlling **$5,000,000 USD or more** in AUM with the software;
- Providing trading, consulting, or advisory services to third parties using
  the software;
- Integrating the software into a commercial product or service;
- Any other use beyond individual personal use.

Commercial License terms and pricing are defined separately by the Licensor.
The Licensor intends commercial pricing to be reasonable. Contact:
westonplatter [at] gmail [dot] com

You are solely responsible for determining whether you qualify for free
Personal Use. The Licensor may request reasonable verification of AUM,
personal-use, or entity status at any time.

## B.4 No Investment Advice

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED FOR EDUCATIONAL AND INFORMATIONAL PURPOSES ONLY. The
software does not constitute investment, financial, legal, or tax advice, does
not create a fiduciary relationship, and does not act as a broker, dealer, or
registered investment advisor. You are solely responsible for all trading
decisions and outcomes.

## B.5 Assumption of Risk

Trading and investing involve substantial risk, including the risk of complete
loss of capital. You use the software entirely at your own risk. The Licensor
is not responsible for any financial losses, including those arising from
market conditions, execution errors, data errors, or software bugs.

## B.6 Indemnification

You agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Licensor from any claims, damages,
liabilities, or expenses arising from your use of the software, your trading
